// Flattened chaos_druid.rs2's [ai_queue3,chaos_druid] table.
// npc_param(death_drop) is unset (null) on this NPC's config, so no
// guaranteed drop.
//
// Two structural simplifications, flagged on #57 (issue #69's Implementation
// Notes: extend minimally and comment rather than silently diverge):
// - Slots 52-62 (11/128) roll ~randomherb TWICE in the source (two obj_add
//   calls in the same branch). The .dropdata format has no way to express
//   "two independent rolls of the same subtable from one branch" - this is
//   collapsed to a single `data=subtable,randomherb,11` row, which
//   under-represents this branch's true herb rate by roughly half.
// - The unholy_symbol_mould branch is gated on `$random < 90 &
//   %itgronigen >= ^itgronigen_complete` - a per-player quest-state
//   conditional, out of scope per the "no quest-state" resolved decision
//   (condition treated as false). Unlike a simple exclusion, treating this
//   compound condition as false means control falls through to the next
//   `else if ($random < 91)` branch for the same random value, so slots
//   89-90 (2/128) resolve to ~randomjewel, not "no drop" - the same
//   fall-through pattern ~randomjewel's own Ring of Wealth/Legends' Quest
//   exclusions already use.
[chaos_druid]
table=drop_table
data=total,128
data=drop,lawrune,2,7
data=drop,airrune,36,3
data=drop,bodyrune,9,2
data=drop,earthrune,9,2
data=drop,mindrune,12,2
data=drop,naturerune,3,1
data=subtable,randomherb,35
data=subtable,randomherb,11
data=drop,coins,3,5
data=drop,coins,8,5
data=drop,coins,29,3
data=drop,coins,35,1
data=drop,vial_water,1,10
data=drop,bronze_longsword,1,1
data=drop,snape_grass,1,1
data=subtable,randomjewel,2
